.TH SPROCKET 1
.SH NAME
sprocket \- a side-scrolling platformer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B games/sprocket
[
.B -t
|
.B -s
] [
.B -q
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sprocket
is a platformer in the shape that genre took:
run and jump with momentum,
a jump whose height depends on how long the button is held,
walkers that turn at a wall or at the edge of what they are standing on
and are dealt with by landing on them,
boxes that give something up when hit from below,
bolts to collect, pits to clear, and a flag at the right-hand end.
.PP
Where
.IR rivet (1)
exercises
.IR nes (2)'s
tile map on a single screen, this exercises the scroll.
The level is 128 tiles wide, drawn once into a surface four screens
across; each frame is a window of that plus whatever is moving.
Hitting a box rewrites one tile in that surface rather than rebuilding
it, which is the point of keeping it around.
.PP
Arrow keys or
.B wasd
to walk;
.BR x ,
.B .
or space to jump, held for height;
.B z
or
.B ,
to run.
.B q
or Escape quits.
.PP
.B -q
starts silent.
.B -t
runs the self test and needs no window.
.B -s
plays a scripted opening headless and writes the composed frame to
.B sprocket.raw
as
.IR w " by " h
of blue, green, red bytes.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
games/sprocket
emu\-cocoa \-r. /dis/games/sprocket.dis \-t
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/games/sprocket.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR nes (2),
.IR rivet (1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B -t
drives the same
.I step
the game loop drives and asserts on game state.
It checks the level's shape and that the walkers came from it;
that the character accelerates, caps at the walk speed, goes faster with
the run button and is stopped by friction;
that a held jump goes higher than a tapped one, which is the whole
difference between this genre and
.IR rivet (1)'s;
that a wall stops it and leaves it outside the wall;
that a pit costs a life;
that a box hit from below is spent and yields a bolt;
that a bolt is collected once and once only;
that landing on a walker flattens it and bounces while running into one
costs a life;
that a walker turns round rather than walking off its ledge;
and that the camera starts clamped, follows, and stops at the far end.
.SH BUGS
There is one course.
Clearing it starts the same one again with the score kept.
.PP
The self test asserts on state, so it cannot see a palette entry that
happens to match the background behind it.
That fault occurred twice while this was written \- the character's
face, then its legs, drawn in colours near enough to the sky to vanish \-
and both times only
.B -s
and a look at the result found it.
.PP
A walker knocked off the level by nothing in particular simply
disappears when it falls past the bottom; it does not come back.
